From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:02:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: Load robust uniforms without a branch

A robust uniform buffer load became off < size ? *(base + off) : 0 in
MSL, which puts every load in a branch of its own, and Metal keeps the
branches. Horizon Zero Dawn's full-screen lighting pass reads 400
constants this way: it took 15-16 ms per frame on an M3, and 2 ms with
robustness turned off.

The loads now read unconditionally, from the device's zero buffer when
the offset is out of bounds, and select the result. The values are the
same, and a null or unwritten descriptor reads the zero buffer rather
than address 0. The root descriptor table carries the zero buffer's
address. Horizon's pass now takes 2-2.5 ms and the fragment work of a
frame 36 instead of 51 ms.

